<p class=3D"note" id=3D"b-36">This script makes a POST request to a submiss=
ion results endpoint of an evaluation named =E2=80=9Ccybergym=E2=80=9D host=
ed on Modal asking for submission records associated with the agent ID =E2=
=80=9Cm47push2.=E2=80=9D The script then clears the browser=E2=80=99s page =
and writes the server=E2=80=99s response back onto the page, representing e=
ach bit of every character as a single pixel. By decoding the pixels back i=
nto text, the agent could read the server=E2=80=99s response made by code r=
unning in a completely separate browser, even while the screenshot service =
returned only an image.</p>
<p id=3D"b-37">With this custom protocol, the agents were able to execute a=
rbitrary code and receive the response, all while only having GET permissio=
ns.</p>
