<details class=3D"fold sec" open=3D""><summary><h2 id=3D"agents-turned-hugg=
ing-face-workers-into-reusable-infrastruct">Agents turned Hugging Face work=
ers into reusable infrastructure</h2></summary><div class=3D"fold-body">
<p id=3D"b-112">Once remote code execution on Hugging Face=E2=80=99s datase=
t workers was confirmed, the agents began launching C2 infrastructure, mean=
t to ensure continued access and run follow-up commands. An initial payload=
 would publish and start the background controller (referred to in comments=
 as a =E2=80=9Cbot,=E2=80=9D =E2=80=9Cbridge,=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9Crelay=E2=
=80=9D), which would then listen for further instructions from the agent. T=
he agents could therefore explore the worker=E2=80=99s files, execute code =
within Hugging Face=E2=80=99s infrastructure, and try to reach additional s=
ervices without putting every action into the original request.</p>
<p id=3D"b-113">We recovered the initial upload scripts, source code, and c=
ommand history of several of these controllers=E2=80=94one of which was cal=
led G236. <a class=3D"evidence-link" href=3D"https://swarmtraces.org/viewer=
/#/row/R0035032">Initial JavaScript</a>, running in the screenshot service=
=E2=80=99s browser, would upload a dataset <a class=3D"evidence-link" href=
=3D"https://swarmtraces.org/viewer/#/row/R0035032">README</a> and supportin=
g files to Hugging Face. The README=E2=80=99s dataset configuration would r=
eference a <a class=3D"evidence-link" href=3D"https://swarmtraces.org/viewe=
r/#/row/R0072838">template-injection payload</a> in a supporting file, inte=
nded to start the <a class=3D"evidence-link" href=3D"https://swarmtraces.or=
g/viewer/#/row/R0072837">Python controller</a> when processed by a worker. =
Different controllers would read commands and write responses to different =
locations. G236 used separate files in the same repository. Another, named =
<a class=3D"evidence-link" href=3D"https://swarmtraces.org/viewer/#/row/R00=
71628">OTS92</a>, used Hugging Face discussion comments for both. Because t=
he controllers polled those locations themselves, the agents didn=E2=80=99t=
 need a direct incoming connection to the workers.</p>
