<p id=3D"b-124">The reusable infrastructure recovered from our data also su=
ggests the agents built deliberate machinery for managing duplicate copies =
of controllers running on possibly different workers, or even sharing a fil=
esystem. These duplicate controllers would poll commands from the same plac=
e, potentially interfering with or repeating work. Controllers and instruct=
ions therefore contained mechanisms to select a surviving copy, stop unwant=
ed ones, and replace a controller that appeared to have died. Some controll=
ers would attempt to prune preexisting copies on startup, others received i=
nstructions to do so after launching.</p>
